From 879bc2ca5399f76932b8c43b0e23b1e67c8fad61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:42:47 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 188/230] design(type): 4-step type scale (xs/sm/md/lg/display)
 replacing 12 ad-hoc sizes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tokens --type-xs/sm/md/lg/display live in tokens.css (named --type-* so the
Tailwind v4 --text-* namespace never self-references) and map to text-xs/sm/
md/lg/display utilities in index.css. All 140 arbitrary pixel size classes
(9/10/11/13/15/18/28/40/48px) are swept to the named scale; the Login clamp()
stays (responsive display, not part of the scale). The text-[color:...] colour
utilities become named colour utilities instead: text-live for the live state,
and a new --text-on-volt token for ink on a volt surface. The date chip needs
that one — the sweep's blind size rewrite turned its colour utility into
text-base, which is a font size, leaving light ink on volt at 2.13:1; the
named ink holds 7.95:1. The FA floor override now targets .text-xs (a no-op
at 12px, kept as a guarantee).

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
